# Generated runtime state for the authorization probe. NONE of this is reviewable and one part of
# it is actively dangerous to commit.
#
# chrome-profile/ is a real Chromium user-data directory created by launchPersistentContext. It has
# contained "Login Data" and "Login Data For Account" — the browser's credential store — plus session
# cookies for a signed-in admin. Committing it would put working authentication material into Git
# history, where deleting the file later does not remove it. It is ~11 MB and 200+ files.
#
# shots-authz/ holds screenshots and responses.json from a run: evidence for the run that produced
# them, not for any later one, and it goes stale the moment the app changes.
chrome-profile/
shots-authz/

# Nothing else in this directory is generated: authz-probe.mjs, run.sh and README.md are reviewed
# source and must stay tracked. The ignore list is deliberately narrow for that reason — a broad
# pattern here would quietly hide the probe's own logic, which is exactly what has to be reviewable
# for its results to mean anything.
